{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And when Moses had finished speaking with them, he put a veil over his face.</b> The verse teaches you that when Moses spoke with Israel — explicating the commandments — he spoke with them without a veil and without any screen at all, and likewise when he spoke with the Holy One, blessed be He. And what it says, ״ובבא משה אל אהל מועד לדבר אתו״ — 'and when Moses came to the Tent of Meeting to speak with Him' — is a narration of a practice that he observed continually after the giving of the Torah, and the verse informs us that from that day onward he conducted himself thus with Israel all his days: when Moses came to the Tent of Meeting he would remove the veil, and when he departed from there he would also go out without a veil and speak with the children of Israel that which he would be commanded; but when he would conclude his discourse with Israel, he would restore the veil upon his face, so that their eyes would not feed upon the radiance that was on his face outside the time of his discourse with them." "<b>And behold,</b> the excellence of this perceptible radiance in the skin of his face, from the day he acquired it at Mount Sinai, never departed from him, but was with him all the days of his life; and even on the day of his death the verse testified concerning him (Deuteronomy 34:7): ״לא כהתה עינו ולא נס לחה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:10.089783479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}